<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F4.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="S3.F4.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> Samples from <em id="S3.F4.8.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">LDMs</em> trained on CelebAHQ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">DBLP:journals/corr/abs-1710-10196</a></cite>, FFHQ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">stylegan</a></cite>, LSUN-Churches <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib102" title="" class="ltx_ref">DBLP:journals/corr/YuZSSX15</a></cite>, LSUN-Bedrooms <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib102" title="" class="ltx_ref">DBLP:journals/corr/YuZSSX15</a></cite> and class-conditional ImageNet <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">DBLP:conf/cvpr/DengDSLL009</a></cite>, each with a resolution of <math id="S3.F4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256\times 256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>256</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256\times 256</annotation></semantics></math>. Best viewed when zoomed in. For more samples <em id="S3.F4.8.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">cf</em>.<span id="S3.F4.8.3" class="ltx_text"></span> the supplement. </span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Conditioning Mechanisms</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Similar to other types of generative
models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">DBLP:journals/corr/MirzaO14</a>; <a href="#bib.bib83" title="" class="ltx_ref">NIPS2015_8d55a249</a></cite>, diffusion models
are in principle capable of modeling conditional distributions of the form
<math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(z|y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(z|y)</annotation></semantics></math>.
This can be implemented with
a conditional denoising autoencoder <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\theta}(z_{t},t,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\theta}(z_{t},t,y)</annotation></semantics></math> and
paves the way to controlling the synthesis process through
inputs <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> such as text <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">Reed2016GenerativeAT</a></cite>, semantic maps  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">spade</a>; <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">DBLP:conf/cvpr/IsolaZZE17</a></cite> or other image-to-image translation tasks <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Isola2017ImagetoImageTW</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In the context of image synthesis, however, combining the
generative power of DMs with other types of conditionings beyond class-labels <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">DBLP:journals/corr/abs-2105-05233</a></cite>
or blurred variants
of the input image <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">DBLP:journals/corr/abs-2104-07636</a></cite>
is so far an under-explored area of research.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We turn DMs into more flexible conditional image generators by
augmenting their underlying UNet backbone with the cross-attention mechanism <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib97" title="" class="ltx_ref">DBLP:conf/nips/VaswaniSPUJGKP17</a></cite>,
which
is
effective for learning attention-based models of various input modalities <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">DBLP:conf/icml/JaegleGBVZC21</a>; <a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">DBLP:journals/corr/abs-2107-14795</a></cite>.
To pre-process <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> from various modalities (such as language prompts) we introduce a domain specific
encoder <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> that projects <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> to an intermediate representation <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\theta}(y)\in\mathbb{R}^{M\times d_{\tau}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\theta}(y)\in\mathbb{R}^{M\times d_{\tau}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which
is then mapped to the intermediate layers of the UNet via a cross-attention
layer implementing <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Attention}(Q,K,V)=\text{softmax}\left(\frac{QK^{T}}{\sqrt{d}}\right)\cdot V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Attention</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Attention}(Q,K,V)=\text{softmax}\left(\frac{QK^{T}}{\sqrt{d}}\right)\cdot V</annotation></semantics></math>, with</p>
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=W^{(i)}_{Q}\cdot\varphi_{i}(z_{t}),\;K=W^{(i)}_{K}\cdot\tau_{\theta}(y),\;V=W^{(i)}_{V}\cdot\tau_{\theta}(y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=W^{(i)}_{Q}\cdot\varphi_{i}(z_{t}),\;K=W^{(i)}_{K}\cdot\tau_{\theta}(y),\;V=W^{(i)}_{V}\cdot\tau_{\theta}(y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{i}(z_{t})\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times d^{i}_{\epsilon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{i}(z_{t})\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times d^{i}_{\epsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes a (flattened) intermediate representation of the UNet implementing
<math id="S3.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{(i)}_{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d^{i}_{\epsilon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{(i)}_{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d^{i}_{\epsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{(i)}_{Q}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d_{\tau}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{(i)}_{Q}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d_{\tau}}</annotation></semantics></math> &amp; <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{(i)}_{K}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d_{\tau}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{(i)}_{K}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d_{\tau}}</annotation></semantics></math> are learnable projection matrices <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib97" title="" class="ltx_ref">DBLP:conf/nips/VaswaniSPUJGKP17</a>; <a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">DBLP:conf/icml/JaegleGBVZC21</a></cite>. See Fig. <a href="#S3.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 3.2 Latent Diffusion Models ‣ 3 Method ‣ High-Resolution Image Synthesis with Latent Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> for a visual depiction.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Based on image-conditioning pairs, we then learn the conditional LDM via</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{LDM}:=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{E}(x),y,\epsilon\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1),t}\Big[\|\epsilon-\epsilon_{\theta}(z_{t},t,\tau_{\theta}(y))\|_{2}^{2}\Big]\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.170em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{LDM}:=\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{E}(x),y,\epsilon\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1),t}\Big[\|\epsilon-\epsilon_{\theta}(z_{t},t,\tau_{\theta}(y))\|_{2}^{2}\Big]\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where
both <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> are jointly optimized via Eq. <a href="#S3.E3" title="Equation 3 ‣ 3.3 Conditioning Mechanisms ‣ 3 Method ‣ High-Resolution Image Synthesis with Latent Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.
This conditioning mechanism is flexible as <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> can be parameterized with domain-specific experts,
<em id="S3.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">e.g</em>.<span id="S3.SS3.p4.2.2" class="ltx_text"></span> (unmasked) transformers <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib97" title="" class="ltx_ref">DBLP:conf/nips/VaswaniSPUJGKP17</a></cite> when <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> are
text prompts (see Sec. <a href="#S4.SS3.SSS1" title="4.3.1 Transformer Encoders for LDMs ‣ 4.3 Conditional Latent Diffusion ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ High-Resolution Image Synthesis with Latent Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3.1</span></a>)</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Experiments</h2>

<figure id="S4.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<table id="S4.F5.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S4.F5.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.F5.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:1.0pt;padding-right:1.0pt;" colspan="7"><span id="S4.F5.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Text-to-Image Synthesis on LAION. 1.45B Model.</span></th></tr>
<tr id="S4.F5.3.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.F5.3.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:1.0pt;padding-right:1.0pt;">
<span id="S4.F5.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block">
<span id="S4.F5.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S4.F5.3.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:50%;">’A street sign that reads</em><span id="S4.F5.3.2.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></span>
<span id="S4.F5.3.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><em id="S4.F5.3.2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:50%;">“Latent Diffusion” ’</em></span>
</span></th>
<th id="S4.F5.3.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:1.0pt;padding-right:1.0pt;">
