<section id="A4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.5 </span>Sample Quality vs. V100 Days (Continued from Sec. <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 On Perceptual Compression Tradeoffs ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ High-Resolution Image Synthesis with Latent Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>)</h3>

<figure id="A4.F17" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F17.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel"><img src="/html/2112.10752/assets/img/compression_analysis/fid_vs_v100d_cin.jpg" id="A4.F17.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" width="685" height="367" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F17.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel"><img src="/html/2112.10752/assets/img/compression_analysis/is_vs_v100d_cin.jpg" id="A4.F17.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" width="685" height="511" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F17.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 17</span>: </span><span id="A4.F17.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> For completeness we also report the training progress of class-conditional <em id="A4.F17.5.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">LDMs</em> on the ImageNet dataset for a fixed number of 35 V100 days.
Results obtained with 100 DDIM steps <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib84" title="" class="ltx_ref">DBLP:conf/iclr/SongME21</a></cite> and <math id="A4.F17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=0</annotation></semantics></math>. FIDs computed on 5000 samples for efficiency reasons.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the assessment of sample quality over the training progress in Sec. <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 On Perceptual Compression Tradeoffs ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ High-Resolution Image Synthesis with Latent Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, we reported FID and IS scores as a function of train steps. Another possibility is to report these metrics over the used resources in V100 days. Such an analysis is additionally provided in Fig. <a href="#A4.F17" title="Figure 17 ‣ D.5 Sample Quality vs. V100 Days (Continued from Sec. ) ‣ Appendix D Additional Results ‣ High-Resolution Image Synthesis with Latent Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>, showing qualitatively similar results.</p>
</div>
</section>
