<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Implementation Details</h3>

<section id="A5.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">E.2.1 </span>Implementations of <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> for conditional <em id="A5.SS2.SSS1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">LDMs</em></h4>

<div id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the experiments on text-to-image and layout-to-image (Sec. <a href="#S4.SS3.SSS1" title="4.3.1 Transformer Encoders for LDMs ‣ 4.3 Conditional Latent Diffusion ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ High-Resolution Image Synthesis with Latent Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3.1</span></a>) synthesis,
we implement the conditioner <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> as an unmasked transformer which processes
a tokenized version of the input <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> and produces an output <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta:=\tau_{\theta}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta:=\tau_{\theta}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>,
where <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta\in\mathbb{R}^{M\times d_{\tau}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta\in\mathbb{R}^{M\times d_{\tau}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
More specifically, the transformer is implemented from <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> transformer blocks consisting of
global self-attention layers, layer-normalization and
position-wise MLPs as follows<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
                
                
                
                
                
                
                
              adapted from <a target="_blank" href="https://github.com/lucidrains/x-transformers" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/lucidrains/x-transformers</a></span></span></span>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A5.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\zeta\leftarrow\text{TokEmb}(y)+\text{PosEmb(y)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>TokEmb</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mtext>PosEmb(y)</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\zeta\leftarrow\text{TokEmb}(y)+\text{PosEmb(y)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{for }i=1,\dots,N:" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{for }i=1,\dots,N:</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\zeta_{1}\leftarrow\text{LayerNorm}(\zeta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>LayerNorm</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\zeta_{1}\leftarrow\text{LayerNorm}(\zeta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\zeta_{2}\leftarrow\text{MultiHeadSelfAttention}(\zeta_{1})+\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>MultiHeadSelfAttention</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\zeta_{2}\leftarrow\text{MultiHeadSelfAttention}(\zeta_{1})+\zeta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\zeta_{3}\leftarrow\text{LayerNorm}(\zeta_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>LayerNorm</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\zeta_{3}\leftarrow\text{LayerNorm}(\zeta_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\zeta\leftarrow\text{MLP}(\zeta_{3})+\zeta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>MLP</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\zeta\leftarrow\text{MLP}(\zeta_{3})+\zeta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\zeta\leftarrow\text{LayerNorm}(\zeta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>LayerNorm</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\zeta\leftarrow\text{LayerNorm}(\zeta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">With <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math> available, the conditioning is mapped into the UNet via the cross-attention mechanism
as depicted in Fig. <a href="#S3.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 3.2 Latent Diffusion Models ‣ 3 Method ‣ High-Resolution Image Synthesis with Latent Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. We modify the “ablated UNet” <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">DBLP:journals/corr/abs-2105-05233</a></cite> architecture
and replace the self-attention layer with a shallow (unmasked) transformer consisting
of <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> blocks with alternating layers of (i) self-attention, (ii) a position-wise MLP and
(iii) a cross-attention layer; see Tab. <a href="#A5.T16" title="Table 16 ‣ E.2.1 Implementations of 
            
              
                
                τ
                θ
              
            
           for conditional LDMs ‣ E.2 Implementation Details ‣ Appendix E Implementation Details and Hyperparameters ‣ High-Resolution Image Synthesis with Latent Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>. Note that without (ii) and (iii), this
architecture is equivalent to the “ablated UNet”.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">While it would be possible to increase the representational power of <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>
by additionally conditioning on the time step <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, we do not pursue this choice as it reduces the speed of inference.
We leave a more detailed analysis of this modification to future work.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">For the text-to-image model, we rely on a publicly available<span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
                
                
                
                
                
                
                
              <a target="_blank" href="https://huggingface.co/transformers/model_doc/bert.html#berttokenizerfast" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/transformers/model_doc/bert.html#berttokenizerfast</a></span></span></span> tokenizer
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib99" title="" class="ltx_ref">DBLP:journals/corr/abs-1910-03771</a></cite>.
The layout-to-image model discretizes the spatial locations of the bounding boxes
and encodes each box as a <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(l,b,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(l,b,c)</annotation></semantics></math>-tuple, where <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the (discrete) top-left and <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> the
bottom-right position. Class information is contained in <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">See Tab. <a href="#A5.T17" title="Table 17 ‣ E.2.1 Implementations of 
            
              
                
                τ
                θ
              
            
           for conditional LDMs ‣ E.2 Implementation Details ‣ Appendix E Implementation Details and Hyperparameters ‣ High-Resolution Image Synthesis with Latent Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a> for the hyperparameters of <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and Tab. <a href="#A5.T13" title="Table 13 ‣ E.1 Hyperparameters ‣ Appendix E Implementation Details and Hyperparameters ‣ High-Resolution Image Synthesis with Latent Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> for those of the UNet for both of the above tasks.
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Note that the class-conditional model as described in Sec. <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 On Perceptual Compression Tradeoffs ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ High-Resolution Image Synthesis with Latent Diffusion Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> is also implemented via cross-attention, where <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is a single learnable
embedding layer with a dimensionality of 512, mapping classes <math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> to
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times 512}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>512</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta\in\mathbb{R}^{1\times 512}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T16" class="ltx_table">
<div id="A5.T16.3" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_pruned_first">
            
<div id="A5.T16.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent ltx_align_center">
<p id="A5.T16.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.T16.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">
<span id="A5.T16.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:144.4pt;height:109.2pt;vertical-align:-52.6pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A5.T16.p2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.T16.p2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">
<span id="A5.T16.p2.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
